Streaming Service
-> where we will be storing (file system/blob)
   what is blob storage ? blob stands for binary large object
   a blob is simply a file , it could be an image , an MP3 song , a video , a PDF , a zip file.
   so blob storage is a storage system designed to store large files , not structured records like a
   database.
   
   drawbacks of storing songs in file system :-
         -> scalibility :- disk space is limited. what happens if you hit 5000 GB ?
         -> durability :- if disk/server crashes , files are lost
         -> replication :- you'd need to manually replicate files to other disks or servers
         -> latency :- serving files to users far from your server adds latency
         -> backups :- no built-in versioning or backup mechanisms.
         -> no cdn :- no caching , geo-replication , etc.
   why blob storage rocks ?
         -> massive scale :- store billion of objects , no size limit per object
         -> highly durable :- 99.999999999% durability (11 9's) - your files are replicated
         -> globally available :- integrated with CDNs (cloudfront/akamai) - fast 
         -> versioning :- can store multiple versions of file
         -> access control :- pre-signed URLs , role-based access
         -> pay as you go :- only pay for what you store and serve
         -> streaming support :- range requests , progressive delivery of audio chunks 

