manifest files -> it manages the different segments of a song for each song version (like 96,160,320) so , 
   in manifest format -> song_96.m3u8 , song_160.m3u8 , song_320.m3u8

now, we are dividing file to different segments so that it will support jump/seek.

different segments , versions and manifest files are stored in S3 storage. (in S3 storage , everything is stored as object.)

each segment is a small binary audio file (object in S3). And we store each binary audio file as a seperate object in S3.
In Blob Storage (like S3) , each file you upload is an "object". 

so, in this technique , user clicks on play button , several segments from s3 using pre-signed url is stored in the client's storage.
and from that storage , one by one sequentially , the segment runs.

user clicks on pause button -> then the client stop requesting different segments from cdn and s3 storage.
                               and also the segment's in client's memory remains as it is.
user clicks on skip button -> all the segments present are flushed in buffer, and new segments and manifest_files are served ,
                              depending upon the current network requirement.



